{"id":"d2ab3c6a8160fff4","group":"62","path":"62/62-thm-Pi1-CA0-perfect-kernel.md","title":"Pi-One-One Comprehension and Perfect Kernels","display":"thm-Pi1-CA0-perfect-kernel — Pi-One-One Comprehension and Perfect Kernels","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)","book_abbrev":"62","label":"62-thm-Pi1-CA0-perfect-kernel","aliases":["62-thm-Pi1-CA0-perfect-kernel"],"display":"thm-Pi1-CA0-perfect-kernel — Pi-One-One Comprehension and Perfect Kernels","depends_on":["[[62-df-RCA0]]","[[62-df-Pi1-CA0]]","[[62-df-Tree]]","[[62-df-perfect-tree]]","[[62-df-equivalence-over-base]]","[[62-thm-pi11-CA0-equivalences]]"],"source":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Theorem VI.1.3","source_pages":[218,219],"source_pdf_pages":[236,237]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"62"},{"key":"label","html":"62-thm-Pi1-CA0-perfect-kernel"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>62-thm-Pi1-CA0-perfect-kernel</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-Pi1-CA0-perfect-kernel — Pi-One-One Comprehension and Perfect Kernels"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dd5e8930337c8b20\" href=\"?note=dd5e8930337c8b20\" title=\"62-df-RCA0\">62-df-RCA0</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2d44fbf8bf7ebe4d\" href=\"?note=2d44fbf8bf7ebe4d\" title=\"62-df-Pi1-CA0\">62-df-Pi1-CA0</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bb825000fd9a8272\" href=\"?note=bb825000fd9a8272\" title=\"62-df-Tree\">62-df-Tree</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"c45c7513cbdebbfa\" href=\"?note=c45c7513cbdebbfa\" title=\"62-df-perfect-tree\">62-df-perfect-tree</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"781620ab41bfeebd\" href=\"?note=781620ab41bfeebd\" title=\"62-df-equivalence-over-base\">62-df-equivalence-over-base</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"c2f8e5f44929f679\" href=\"?note=c2f8e5f44929f679\" title=\"62-thm-pi11-CA0-equivalences\">62-thm-pi11-CA0-equivalences</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source","html":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Theorem VI.1.3"},{"key":"source_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>218</span><span>219</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>236</span><span>237</span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p>理论见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"dd5e8930337c8b20\" href=\"?note=dd5e8930337c8b20\" title=\"62-df-RCA0\">62-df-RCA0</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"2d44fbf8bf7ebe4d\" href=\"?note=2d44fbf8bf7ebe4d\" title=\"62-df-Pi1-CA0\">62-df-Pi1-CA0</a>，树见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"bb825000fd9a8272\" href=\"?note=bb825000fd9a8272\" title=\"62-df-Tree\">62-df-Tree</a>，Kernel 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"c45c7513cbdebbfa\" href=\"?note=c45c7513cbdebbfa\" title=\"62-df-perfect-tree\">62-df-perfect-tree</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}\">\\(\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"781620ab41bfeebd\" href=\"?note=781620ab41bfeebd\" title=\"62-df-equivalence-over-base\">62-df-equivalence-over-base</a>；树路径指标刻画见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"c2f8e5f44929f679\" href=\"?note=c2f8e5f44929f679\" title=\"62-thm-pi11-CA0-equivalences\">62-thm-pi11-CA0-equivalences</a>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PK}\">\\(\\mathrm{PK}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PK}_2\">\\(\\mathrm{PK}_2\\)</span> 在下式引入。</p>\n<p>上游理论为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RCA}_0,\\Pi^1_1\\text{-}\\mathrm{CA}_0\">\\(\\mathrm{RCA}_0,\\Pi^1_1\\text{-}\\mathrm{CA}_0\\)</span>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}Pi1\\text{-}CA0\\text{-}perfect\\text{-}kernel}\\vdash\\;\\mathrm{PK}\\coloneqq\\forall T(\\mathsf{Tree}(T)\\to\\exists P\\;\\mathsf{Kernel}(P,T)),\\qquad\n\\mathrm{PK}_2\\coloneqq\\forall T(\\operatorname{BinTree}(T)\\to\\exists P\\;\\mathsf{Kernel}(P,T)).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}Pi1\\text{-}CA0\\text{-}perfect\\text{-}kernel}\\vdash\\;\\mathrm{PK}\\coloneqq\\forall T(\\mathsf{Tree}(T)\\to\\exists P\\;\\mathsf{Kernel}(P,T)),\\qquad\n\\mathrm{PK}_2\\coloneqq\\forall T(\\operatorname{BinTree}(T)\\to\\exists P\\;\\mathsf{Kernel}(P,T)).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\Pi^1_1\\text{-}\\mathrm{CA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{PK}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0),\\\\\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\Pi^1_1\\text{-}\\mathrm{CA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{PK}_2\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\Pi^1_1\\text{-}\\mathrm{CA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{PK}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0),\\\\\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\Pi^1_1\\text{-}\\mathrm{CA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{PK}_2\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>正向形成能延伸到非空完美子树的结点集。反向把每个 Tᵢ 与任意辅助数标签配对，使其有路径恰好对应新树有非空完美子树；再将所有 i 分支及自然数标签编码到二叉树。完美核中各标志结点的成员关系给出全部路径指标，应用 VI.1.1。二叉完美核原则与二叉 WKL 的区别在“形成所有分支的最大完美部分”，非仅选一条路径。</p>\n<p>来源：第二版（2009），Theorem VI.1.3；纸面页 218, 219；PDF 页 236, 237。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{